just one day after pro football star  deshawn watson was suspended for six  games to start the new season the nfl is  punishing one of its teams for violating  the integrity of the game policy a  six-month investigation found the miami  dolphins violated tampering rules  speaking with superstar tom brady and an  agent for coach sean payton while they  were under contract with other teams nfl  commissioner roger goodell called the  findings unprecedented this  investigation stems from a lawsuit filed  by former dolphins head coach brian  flores who claims that he was pressured  to lose games  for the miami dolphins players it's  business as usual on the practice field  but behind the scenes the nfl unleashed  a bombshell punishment on the team for  major tampering violations the dolphins  will forfeit their first round pick next  year and the third round pick in 2024  owner stephen ross will be suspended  until after week six of the season  meaning he cannot enter the team  headquarters and he'll pay a 1.5 million  dollar fine you don't normally see a  commissioner come out in a disciplinary  process like that and go after an owner  the way that he did conor orr a staff  writer for sports illustrated says on  the heels of monday's six-game  suspension of cleveland browns  quarterback deshaun watson for  allegations of sexual misconduct the nfl  was put in a unique position the nfl had  wanted to suspend watson for at least a  year but an independent judge settled on  six games they were put in a corner in  terms of  they've never punished owners as  significantly as they were trying to  punish deshaun watson maybe this is why  you're seeing such a change in tone from  goodell and maybe this is why you're  seeing the league be a little less  afraid today in terms of being critical  about other owners the investigation by  the league found the dolphins tried to  recruit tom brady on multiple occasions  while he was under contract with other  teams the team also made contact with an  agent for head coach sean payton while  he was with the saints ross said on the  tampering allegations i strongly  disagree with the conclusions and the  punishment however i will accept the  outcome in the lawsuit that initiated  the investigation former dolphins head  coach brian flores noted the team's  contact with a prominent quarterback and  he also claimed ross offered him 100  thousand dollars for each game he lost  in 2019 so the team could get better  draft picks we spoke to flores in  february after he sued the league this  game you know changed my life uh so to  attack the integrity of the game that's  that's what i felt was happening in that  instance and  i wouldn't stand for it and that was  dolphin's owner steven ross yes  yes but the league's investigation found  the dolphins did not intentionally lose  games in 2019 nor did anyone at the club  including mr ross instruct coach flores  to do so but it notes ross did express  his belief that the team's draft  position should take priority over the  team's win loss record in a statement  nfl commissioner roger goodell said even  if made in jest and not intended to be  taken seriously comments suggesting that  draft position is more important than  winning can be misunderstood ross says  the league cleared the team of flores  allegations and flores said in a  statement i am disappointed to learn  that the investigation minimized mr  ross's offers and pressure to tank games  one note about stephen ross's suspension  it's the same number of games as desean  watson's punishment for allegations of  sexual assault the nfl still can appeal  the arbitrator's decision on watson's  suspension but it must do so by tomorrow  and you wonder i mean ross is 82  billionaire how much of an impact that  really has on him but as a former player  how much of an impact does this have on  the actual team  you know it's it's funny to say but it's  the reality when things happen outside  of the facility and by outside i mean  upstairs above you we call the guys in  the suits coaches owners gm's  we can turn a blind eye if it's not  directly impacting the x's and o's the  play of the quarterback how we operate  on the practice field end on game day  not much  but when they start dealing with issues  let's just say the browns for example  that's a completely different situation  yeah because you're talking about a man  and some serious allegations that could  offend a teammate and then you have to  sit in that locker room with an  individual so now it's up to me as a  teammate to understand who deshawn  watson is do you accept him as a  teammate do you accept what he did or  did not do so they're two separate  situations miami dolphins and the  cleveland browns right yeah
 

